.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VOP_CACHEDLOOKUP 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vop_cachedlookup
.Nd lookup a name in a directory with cache support
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vop_cachedlookup "struct vnode *dvp" "struct vnode **vpp" "struct componentname *cnp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vop_cachedlookup
function searches for a directory entry, first checking the name cache.
If the entry is found in the cache, the associated vnode is returned in
.Fa *vpp .
If not found, it calls
.Xr vop_lookup 9
to perform the lookup on the filesystem.
If the filesystem lookup is successful, the result is added to the name cache.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa cred"
.It Fa dvp
The directory vnode to search.
.It Fa vpp
Pointer to a vnode pointer where the result will be stored.
.It Fa cnp
The component name information for the lookup.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vnode 9 ,
.Xr vop_lookup 9 ,
.Xr cache_lookup 9
